<title>SWITZERLAND: Ciba SC rights drop after bid price set.</title>
<headline>Ciba SC rights drop after bid price set.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Subscription rights for Ciba Specialty Chemical Holding Inc shares came under presure after a bank consortium said it would offer 90 Swiss francs for the rights.</p>
<p>Rights were quoted at 96.00 francs, down 5.50, in heavy volume. They opened at 92.50.</p>
<p>The consortium, led by CSFB and UBS, set its bid price last night. It will use the rights it acquires for a global offering of shares in Ciba, which is being spun off from Novartis in a one-for-one rights issue. Rights end trading tomorrow.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
